### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  The main goal (deliver resources) requires both collecting and delivering resources.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3, G2.4 [SEQUENTIAL (;)]**  
  Collection involves determining storage order, visiting storages, retrieving resources, and handling battery failures in sequence.

- **G2.2 -> AT1 [AND]**  
  Visiting a storage location requires navigating to it (AT1).

- **G2.3 -> AT2 [AND]**  
  Retrieving resources requires requesting them from the storage (AT2).

- **G2.4 -> AT3, AT4 [FALLBACK]**  
  If battery is low during collection, the robot either returns to recharge (AT3) or transfers the task (AT4).

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [SEQUENTIAL (;)]**  
  Delivery involves transporting resources and handling battery failures in sequence.

- **G3.1 -> AT5 [AND]**  
  Delivering resources requires transporting them to the requesting location (AT5).

- **G3.2 -> AT6, AT7 [FALLBACK]**  
  If battery is low during delivery, the robot either returns to a checkpoint (AT6) or alerts the sector manager (AT7).

- **G2.2 -> Multiple AT1s [PARALLEL (#)]**  
  When multiple storages are involved, each storage visit (AT1) is executed in parallel by different robots.
